sman School of Medicine, New York, NY, USA. k.j.geras@nyu.edu."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-5117-9651"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-9284-4830"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-9564-9360"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-0390-3964"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-6076-725X"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-6577-8601"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-7726-2514"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-0549-1446"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0009-0005-8416-1585"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "1", "volume": "12", "journalIssueId": 3226554, "dateOfPublication": "2021 Sep", "monthOfPublication": 9, "yearOfPublication": 2021, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Nat Commun", "title": "Nature communications", "essn": "2041-1723", "issn": "2041-1723", "nlmid": "101528555", "isoabbreviation": "Nat Commun"}, "printPublicationDate": "2021-09-01"}, "pubYear": "2021", "pageInfo": "5645", "abstractText": "Though consistently shown to detect mammographically occult cancers, breast ultrasound has been noted to have high false-positive rates. In this work, we present an AI system that achieves radiologist-level accuracy in identifying breast cancer in ultrasound images. Developed on 288,767 exams, consisting of 5,442,907 B-mode and Color Doppler images, the AI achieves an area under the receiver operating characteristic curve (AUROC) of 0.976 on a test set consisting of 44,755 exams. In a retrospective reader study, the AI achieves a higher AUROC than the average of ten board-certified breast radiologists (AUROC: 0.962 AI, 0.924 ± 0.02 radiologists). With the help of the AI, radiologists decrease their false positive rates by 37.3% and reduce requested biopsies by 27.8%, while maintaining the same level of sensitivity. This highlights the potential of AI in improving the accuracy, consistency, and efficiency of breast ultrasound diagnosis.", "affiliation": "Center for Data Science, New York University, New York, NY, USA.", "publicationStatus": "epublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't", "research-article", "Research Support, U.S. Gov't, Non-P.H.S.", "Journal Article", "Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "U.S. Department of Health &amp; Human Services | National Institutes of Health", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "U.S. Department of Health &amp; Human Services | National Institutes of Health", "grantId": "P41EB017183", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "U.S. Department of Health &amp; Human Services | National Institutes of Health", "grantId": "R21CA225175", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Science Foundation", "grantId": "1922658", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Polish National Agency for Academic Exchange", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "R21 CA225175", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Gordon and Betty Moore Foundation", "grantId": "9683", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Breast", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "DG", "qualifierName": "diagnostic imaging"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Breast Neoplasms", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "DG", "qualifierName": "diagnostic imaging"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "DI", "qualifierName": "diagnosis"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Mammography", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "MT", "qualifierName": "methods"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Ultrasonography", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "MT", "qualifierName": "methods"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", 